    caseText: `
    <p>Quantum Robotics Ltd. is developing a compact robotic inspection unit for automobile component
    manufacturers. The market is highly competitive and customers have indicated that they will not
    pay more than <strong>₹12 lakh</strong> per unit for the proposed specification. The company wants
    to earn a profit of <strong>₹2.16 lakh</strong> per unit.</p>
    <p>The preliminary cost model estimates direct material at ₹4.20 lakh, direct labour at ₹1.50 lakh,
    manufacturing overhead at ₹1.20 lakh, software and testing at ₹0.90 lakh, installation and training
    at ₹0.50 lakh, and warranty/service cost at ₹0.40 lakh per unit.</p>
    <p>Before the product is finalised, the engineering team identifies a potential cost reduction of
    ₹0.30 lakh through redesign of the robotic arm. A supplier also offers a redesigned sensor module
    that reduces material cost by ₹0.25 lakh but increases testing cost by ₹0.08 lakh.</p>
    <p>After launch, the company expects one assembly station to become a bottleneck. The station will
    have 900 available minutes per week. Product R requires 15 bottleneck minutes and generates
    throughput of ₹600 per unit. Product S requires 20 bottleneck minutes and generates throughput of
    ₹720 per unit. Maximum weekly demand is 40 units of R and 30 units of S.</p>
    <p>The finance team also estimated that product development expenditure before launch will be
    ₹18 lakh and end-of-life recycling costs are expected to be ₹0.10 lakh per unit. The expected
    product life is 2,000 units. Management wants the final decision to reflect the principles of
    target costing, life cycle costing and throughput accounting rather than relying solely on
    conventional departmental cost reports.</p>
    <p>The operations manager nevertheless proposes that both products should be produced in proportion
    to their sales demand because otherwise one production department may appear inefficient. The
    management accountant disagrees, arguing that the constrained assembly station should determine
    the product mix.</p>
    `,
