    caseText: `

      <p>SecureDoor Systems Limited installs and services automated industrial doors
      for warehouses and manufacturing plants. After installation, customers may
      request different types of service, including installation, replacement,
      adjustment and lubrication.</p>

      <p>The Service Manager has noticed that certain components generate substantially
      more service calls than others. Because the company has limited technical
      personnel, it cannot develop specialist expertise for every component and every
      type of service problem simultaneously.</p>

      <p>The company collected service-call information for five major components during
      the latest service period.</p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Component</th>
            <th>Install</th>
            <th>Replace</th>
            <th>Adjust</th>
            <th>Lubricate</th>
            <th>Total</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Door</td><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>12</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Motor</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>18</td><td>7</td><td>30</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Track</td><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>7</td><td>4</td><td>17</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sensor</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Locking Unit</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>9</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>The Service Manager proposes a two-level Pareto Analysis. At the first level,
      components will be ranked according to total service calls. At the second level,
      once the most significant component is identified, the individual service types
      for that component will be ranked separately.</p>

      <p>The objective is to determine where technician training, spare-parts planning
      and preventive-maintenance resources should initially be concentrated.</p>

      <p>The management team understands that the 80:20 principle is not a rigid
      mathematical rule. The important objective is to identify the relatively few
      categories responsible for a substantial share of the total effect.</p>

      <p>Management also intends to repeat the analysis after implementing corrective
      actions. This will help determine whether the original major causes have declined
      and whether another cause has subsequently become significant.</p>
    `,
